{"title":"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2022 AMC 10A #9</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">2022 AMC 12A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Different_Kind_Of_Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Different Kind Of Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Under_a_minute)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (Under a minute)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle is partitioned into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> regions as shown. Each region is to be painted a solid color - red, orange, yellow, blue, or green - so that regions that touch are painted different colors, and colors can be used more than once. How many different colorings are possible?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c53adae322a3fcf0e0d1d0d2aa43ce0ad69527c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5.5cm); draw((0,0)--(0,2)--(2,2)--(2,0)--cycle); draw((2,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(2,2)--cycle); draw((8,0)--(12,0)--(12,2)--(8,2)--cycle); draw((0,2)--(6,2)--(6,4)--(0,4)--cycle); draw((6,2)--(12,2)--(12,4)--(6,4)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"262\" height=\"88\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d96d01999ea6a958f5aa722c187032a2168424b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }120\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }270\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }360\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }540\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }720$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The top left rectangle can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible colors. Then the bottom left region can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible colors, and the bottom middle can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> colors since it is next to the top left and bottom left. Similarly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the top right and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the bottom right, which gives us a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85183d987ed0c2d3e39cbefbe7416511f41ab2ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot4\\cdot3\\cdot3\\cdot3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }540}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"198\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Txu\n</p><p>Note that the number of choices for a rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa98cdb49e9488a46b3ec7267558f612a6a85fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> when there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rectangles adjacent to it. ~GoldemGem4848\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Casework)\">Solution 2 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Case 1: All the rectangles are different colors. It would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a578519da397fe10b98efaa61cb1c65ca1b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5! = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> choices. \n</p><p>Case 2: Two rectangles that are the same color. Grouping these two rectangles as one gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b20cd1e708b2ec9fa5637050de52da54c53e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot4\\cdot3\\cdot2 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />. But, you need to multiply this number by three because the same-colored rectangles can be chosen at the top left and bottom right, the top right and bottom left, or the bottom right and bottom left, which gives us a grand total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62a47cbc153efdf4611d8660429ea879be3f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Case 3: We have two sets of rectangles chosen from these choices (top right &amp; bottom left, top left &amp; bottom right) that have the same color. However, the choice of the bottom left and bottom right does not work for this case, as the second pair would be chosen from two touching rectangles. Again, grouping the same-colored rectangles gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/20667ab55f16df2ec8090f40d15962c35ba6df37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot4\\cdot3 = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8dc62b68d99038ea15b96cc7bd4546af2e53a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 + 360 + 60 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }540}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"218\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~orenbad\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Different_Kind_Of_Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Different_Kind_Of_Casework)\">Solution 3 (Different Kind Of Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Different Kind Of Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us first choose the color of the bottom-middle rectangle, as it is touching all the other rectangles and has to be a different color than all of them. This rectangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities. To make things easier for us, let's assume we chose the color red. Now, lets choose the color of the top-left rectangle. This has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> options: orange, yellow, blue, or green (it can't be the same color as the middle rectangle, which we assumed was red). Lets assume this is orange. Now, we know that the bottom-left rectangle only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices: yellow, blue, or green. Lets assume this is colored yellow. Now, lets do casework on the color of the bottom right-rectangle. It either can be the same color as the top-left (orange), or different.\nCASE 1: (Its the same color)\nWe then know that the bottom-right rectangle is also colored orange. We now know that the top-left rectangle only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices: yellow, blue, or green (it can't be orange or red). The sum of the possibilities of this case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168459a4a05031ba65c3c824366a2264d68579ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot4\\cdot3\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>CASE 2: (Its a different color)\nWe then know that the bottom-right rectangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> options (yellow, blue, or green, since it can't be red, and it can't be orange since we already covered that in the case 1). Lets assume it is colored yellow. We know have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the top-right rectangle (blue or green). The sum of the possibilities of this case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968906015a5a6f2c666e10a5e4baf7409a442115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot4\\cdot3\\cdot3\\cdot2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We can then sum up the possibilities of our two cases, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042692805914d848c99bdf48ea739414c6ed2b59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot4\\cdot3\\cdot3+5\\cdot4\\cdot3\\cdot3\\cdot2 = 5\\cdot4\\cdot3(3+3\\cdot2) = 60\\cdot9 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }540}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"516\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Irfans123\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/d_yfk7pYsSw\">https://youtu.be/d_yfk7pYsSw</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Under_a_minute.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Under_a_minute)\">Video Solution 2 (Under a minute)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (Under a minute)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7yAh4MtJ8a8?si=88gRS7RBVbN7yCng&amp;t=1290\">https://youtu.be/7yAh4MtJ8a8?si=88gRS7RBVbN7yCng&amp;t=1290</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A\">2022 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</